|~ `::fn` and what is declared under it: the function, its constructor,
   the verbs that build it from the noun and the verbs that fill and read
   it, their refusals and their laws. The verbs of this source are written
   as their literal, the chain that builds a function folded into data,
   since none of them stands while the source runs; the chain builds every
   other verb.
   The rules it holds: [QSBLD#fn]. ~|

:fn
  |~~ A function: the subject it runs on, the inputs it takes, the answer
      it gives, the refusals it pages and the facts each wires, the
      invariants it holds, its laws, and its recipe, code or a primitive of
      the host. It is built from the noun by a chain, the commands written
      on it, each a verb the function so far is the subject of, the recipe
      last:
      `::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | impl ~(add by)`.
      `on` names the subject, its page and its kinds; `takes` an input, its
      name, its page, its selector over the args, `/0` the first arg
      and `~(query /0 1)` the first or one, and its kinds; `returns` the
      answer, its page and its kinds; `throws` a refusal, its page and the
      kind of its facts, the quote of its own `wires` or the tag of the
      refusal whose kind it shares; `holds`
      an invariant of the subject, an input or the answer, its refusal, its
      page and its condition; `proves` a law of the function, its page and
      its query; and `impl` the recipe. Each command hands what it is
      written with to the chain, which holds it as it holds the literal.
      An input holds the value of its kind
      the walk of its tags reaches, and a value of none is refused under
      the input. A verb is a function named under a
      label, called by its function alone, and `apply` runs a function on
      its subject with a vector of args, as a call holds its args,
      `5 | apply f [3]`. A function holds no scope: its recipe reads its
      inputs, its subject and the verbs of the tree, and a value it needs
      beside them is an input or is written in its code, which `fill` does.
      It prints as its literal, the chain folded into data, its commands in
      a quote and its recipe after it, and reads back from it.
      ::link~(::any/apply | doc) ::link~(::quote | doc)
      ::link~(::qlang/verbs | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | accepts
        |~~ The literal of a function, the quote of the commands of its
            chain and its recipe, a quote, a primitive, or null for a
            contract no call runs.
        ~~|
    | throws :PayloadNotPairError
        |~~ The literal of a function is a pair, the quote of the commands
            of its chain and its recipe,
            `::fn[~(takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0) ~(add by)]`: a payload
            of another shape, a first that is no quote and a pair under
            another tag among them, is refused.
        ~~|
        ~(wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the value refused. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The value refused. ~~|)
    | throws :CommandNotTakenError
        |~~ Each step of the chain of a function is a command the chain
            takes, written with the modifiers the page of its verb names in
            their order, `::fn/takes | doc` those of `takes`, whether the
            verb wrote it or the literal: `:command` holds the command as
            written, `:index` the index of the modifier refused, from zero,
            or of the first left out, and `:actualValue` the modifier.
            ::link~(::fn/on | doc) ::link~(::fn/takes | doc)
            ::link~(::fn/returns | doc) ::link~(::fn/throws | doc)
            ::link~(::fn/holds | doc)
            ::link~(::fn/proves | doc)
        ~~|
        ~(wires :command |~~ The command as written, a quote of its step. ~~| ::quote
          | wires :index
              |~~ The index, from zero, of the element refused. ~~|
              ~(query /index) #[::null ::number]
          | wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the value refused. ~~| ~(query /actualTag) #[::null ::tag]
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The value refused. ~~| ~(query /actualValue))
    | throws :NameDeclaredTwiceError
        |~~ A name of a chain is declared once: an input, a refusal
            and an invariant each by its name, the subject and the answer
            by theirs, and an invariant names no refusal the kinds of its
            input name, `:by/KindNotTakenError`.
        ~~|
        ~(wires :name |~~ The name asked for, a keyword or a tag. ~~| #[::keyword ::tag]
          | wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the value refused. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The value refused. ~~|)
    | throws :NameUnderNoInputError
        |~~ A refusal or an invariant written with a path is named under
            the subject, an input taken before it or the answer,
            `:by/TooBigError`, and an invariant is written with one.
        ~~|
        ~(wires :name |~~ The name asked for, a keyword or a tag. ~~| #[::keyword ::tag]
          | wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the value refused. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The value refused. ~~|)
    | throws :LawUnderNoNameError
        |~~ A law written with a path is named under a name the function
            declares before it: an input, a refusal, an invariant, a fact,
            the subject or the answer, the refusal an input's kinds name
            among them, `proves :by/KindNotTakenError/refusesAString …`.
        ~~|
        ~(wires :name |~~ The name asked for, a keyword or a tag. ~~| #[::keyword ::tag]
          | wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the value refused. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The value refused. ~~|)
    | throws :RecipeKindNotTakenError
        |~~ The recipe is a quote, a primitive of the host, or null for a
            contract, whether `impl` gives it or the literal writes it.
        ~~|
        ::kind/KindNotTakenError
    | throws :RecipeMissingError
        |~~ A function runs the recipe it holds: a contract holds none, and
            a `::builtin{}` runs the primitive a host handed with the
            function that holds it, or with the function equal to it the
            root holds at the address its `:of` names, so a function of a
            host read back from its print runs it, while one written by a
            reader or put into a function of its own runs nothing. `impl`
            gives a function code, `| impl ~(add by)`.
        ~~|
        ~(wires :of
              |~~ The address the descriptor of the recipe names: where the root
                  holds no function equal to the one refused.
              ~~|
              ~(query /of) #[::null ::tag]
          | wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the value refused. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The value refused. ~~|)
    | throws :KindNotTakenError
        |~~ A value an input reads of none of the kinds it takes, or one
            that is no vector where it takes the kinds of each element, is
            refused under the input, `::number/add/addend/KindNotTakenError`,
            and an answer of none of the kinds `returns` names under the
            answer: every such refusal is closed by the kind of this one, the
            page of each standing under its own verb, and a refusal a
            primitive raises of a value of none of the kinds it takes shares
            it by its tag, `::vec/filter/ConditionKindNotTakenError`.
            ::link~(::fn/takes | doc) ::link~(::fn/returns | doc)
        ~~|
        ~(wires :repair
              |~~ The step the call was likely meant as: where it gave a path
                  for the value the path names, `mul (get /qty)` for
                  `mul /qty`, and null where it gave none.
              ~~|
              ~(query /repair) #[::null ::quote]
          | wires :expected |~~ The kinds taken. ~~| ::set
          | wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the value refused. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The value refused. ~~|)
    | throws :ElementKindNotTakenError
        |~~ An element of none of the kinds an input takes for each element
            is refused under the input, `::vec/concat/vectors/ElementKindNotTakenError`,
            the first element so refused: every such refusal is closed by the
            kind of this one, and a refusal a primitive raises of an element
            of none of the kinds it takes shares it by its tag,
            `::any/allOf/ConditionKindNotTakenError`.
            ::link~(::fn/takes | doc)
        ~~|
        ~(wires :index |~~ The index, from zero, of the first element refused. ~~| ::number
          | wires :expected |~~ The kinds each element takes. ~~| ::set
          | wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the element refused. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The element refused. ~~|)
    | throws :NotGivenError
        |~~ An input the args of the call leave out is refused under the
            input, `::vec/map/code/NotGivenError`, the args its
            `actualValue`: every such refusal is closed by the kind of this
            one.
            ::link~(::fn/takes | doc)
        ~~|
        ~(wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the args, the address of the verb. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The args of the call, under the address of the verb. ~~|)
    | throws :ArgsBeyondInputsError
        |~~ Args past those the inputs of a verb read are refused under the
            verb, `::number/add/ArgsBeyondInputsError`: every such refusal is
            closed by the kind of this one.
            ::link~(::fn/takes | doc)
        ~~|
        ~(wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the args, the address of the verb. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :arity |~~ How many args the inputs read. ~~| ::number
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The args of the call, under the address of the verb. ~~|)
    | throws :SubjectRefusedError
        |~~ A subject the verb does not serve, of none of the kinds its
            label and `on` name, is refused under the verb as
            `SubjectNot` and the label, `::number/add/SubjectNotNumberError`,
            and a subject an invariant of the subject does not hold of under
            the name the invariant gives: every such refusal is closed by the
            kind of this one, the first frame of its trace holding the
            subject, and a refusal a primitive raises of its subject shares
            it by its tag, `::string/toNumber/TextNotNumberError`.
            ::link~(::fn/on | doc) ::link~(::fn/holds | doc)
        ~~|
        ~(wires :repair
              |~~ The step the call was likely meant as: where the subject is
                  a path for the value it names, `get /tags | count` for
                  `/tags | count`, and null where it is none.
              ~~|
              ~(query /repair) #[::null ::quote]
          | wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the subject refused. ~~| ::tag)
    | throws :InvariantNotHeldError
        |~~ An input or an answer an invariant of the function does not hold
            of is refused under the name the invariant gives,
            `::number/div/divisor/ZeroError`: every such refusal is closed by
            the kind of this one.
            ::link~(::fn/holds | doc)
        ~~|
        ~(wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the value refused. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The input or the answer the invariant refused. ~~|)
    | proves :KindNotTakenError/readsTheFactsByTheirNames
        |~~ A value an input refuses answers its kinds, its kind and itself
            by their names.
        ~~|
        ~(1 | add "x" !| get [~(expected) ~(actualTag) ~(actualValue)] | eq [#[::number] ::string "x"])
    | proves :KindNotTakenError/namesTheRepairOfAPath
        |~~ A path the call gives for the value it names names the step
            that reads it.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | mul /qty !| repair | eq ~(mul (get /qty)))
    | proves :KindNotTakenError/namesNoRepairOfAPathANameHolds
        |~~ A path a name holds is no path the step wrote, and names no
            repair.
        ~~|
        ~(:p /qty | 5 | mul p !| repair | eq null)
    | proves :KindNotTakenError/namesNoRepairOfAPathADefaultReads
        |~~ A path an input reads by default is no path the step wrote, and
            names no repair.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| ~(query /0 /one) ::number | impl ~(add by)) | 5 | plus !| repair | eq null)
    | proves :ElementKindNotTakenError/readsTheIndexOfTheElement
        |~~ An element an input refuses answers its index. ~~|
        ~([1] | concat [2] 3 !| get [~(index) ~(actualValue)] | eq [1 3])
    | proves :NotGivenError/readsTheArgs
        |~~ An input the args leave out answers the args of the call. ~~|
        ~([1 2] | map !| actualValue | eq ::vec/map[])
    | proves :ArgsBeyondInputsError/readsTheArity
        |~~ Args past the inputs answer how many the inputs read. ~~|
        ~(1 | add 1 2 !| get [~(arity) ~(actualValue)] | eq [1 ::number/add[1 2]])
    | proves :SubjectRefusedError/readsTheKindOfTheSubject
        |~~ A subject the verb does not serve answers its kind, the first
            frame of the trace holding it.
        ~~|
        ~("x" | add 1 !| get [~(actualTag) ~(trace | first | subject)] | eq [::string "x"])
    | proves :InvariantNotHeldError/readsTheValueRefused
        |~~ An input an invariant refuses answers itself. ~~|
        ~(10 | div 0 !| actualValue | eq 0)
    | proves :isBuiltByCommands
        |~~ A function is built from the noun. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~(add by) | tag | eq ::fn)
    | proves :printsAsItsLiteral
        |~~ A function prints as its commands and its recipe. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | impl ~(add by) | print | eq "::fn[~(takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number) ~(add by)]")
    | proves :readsBackFromItsPrint
        |~~ The print of a function reads back as the function. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~(add by) | :f it | print | parse | open | eq f)
    | proves :isAVerbNamedUnderALabel
        |~~ A function named under a label is a verb, called by its
            function.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | impl ~(add by)) | 5 | plus 3 | eq 8)
    | proves :pagesTheInputsOfAVerb
        |~~ The page of an input is the page of its node under the verb. ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~(add by)) | ::number/plus/by | doc | content | trim | eq "How much.")
    | proves :runsAPrimitiveRecipe
        |~~ A function whose recipe is a primitive runs it, the verb
            `fill` applied by its value as it is called.
        ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~(add by) | apply (::fn/fill | binding | value) [3] | eq ~(:by |~~ How much. ~~| 3 | add by))
    | proves :holdsTheInvariantsOfAnInput
        |~~ An invariant written under an input refuses a value that
            breaks it.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | holds :by/TooBigError |~~ Under a hundred. ~~| ~(lt 100) | impl ~(add by)) [500]
          !| get [~(tag) /actualValue]
          |  eq [::fn/call/by/TooBigError 500])
    | proves :holdsTheInvariantsOfItsSubject
        |~~ An invariant written under the subject refuses a subject that
            breaks it, before the inputs are read.
        ~~|
        ~(-5 | apply (::fn | holds :subject/NotAboveZeroError |~~ Above zero. ~~| ~(gt 0) | impl ~(add 1)) !| tag | eq ::fn/call/subject/NotAboveZeroError)
    | proves :holdsTheInvariantsOfItsAnswer
        |~~ An invariant written under the answer refuses an answer that
            breaks it.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | holds :answer/TooBigError |~~ A number past ten. ~~| ~(lt 10) | impl ~(add 100))
          !| get [~(tag) /actualValue]
          |  eq [::fn/call/answer/TooBigError 105])
    | proves :answersTheFailureOfACondition
        |~~ A condition that fails answers its failure. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | holds :by/TooBigError |~~ Under a hundred. ~~| ~(get /nope) | impl ~(add by)) [3]
          !| tag
          |  eq ::path/SubjectHasNoPartsError)
    | proves :answersTheFailureOfAModifier
        |~~ A modifier computed at the call that failed is the answer,
            where the input that reads it takes no quote.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | impl ~(add by))
          | :number/one (::fn | returns |~~ One. ~~| ::number | impl ~(1))
          | :number/any (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~(by))
          | :number/bare ~(1)
          | get [~(5 | plus (get /x) !| tag) ~(5 | one (get /x) !| tag) ~(5 | any (get /x) !| tag) ~(5 | bare (get /x) !| tag)]
          | every ~(eq ::path/SubjectHasNoPartsError))
    | proves :PayloadNotPairError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no pair. ~~|
        ~(::fn[1] !| tag | eq ::fn/PayloadNotPairError)
    | proves :PayloadNotPairError/refusesCommandsThatAreNoQuote
        |~~ The commands of a chain are a quote. ~~|
        ~(::fn[[] ~(1)] !| tag | eq ::fn/PayloadNotPairError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesACommandItsVerbWrites
        |~~ A command its verb writes with what the chain does not take is
            refused as the literal's is, the command its `:actualValue`.
        ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes 5 |~~ x ~~| /0 !| get [~(tag) ~(command) ~(index) ~(actualValue)] | eq [::fn/CommandNotTakenError ~(takes 5 |~~ x ~~| /0) 0 5])
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/countsTheObjectsAsTheLiteralDoes
        |~~ A command its verb writes with a modifier left out or past the
            last is refused as the literal's is.
        ~~|
        ~(get [~(::fn | takes :by |~~ x ~~| !| index) ~(::fn[~(takes :by |~~ x ~~|) null] !| index) ~(::fn | takes :by |~~ x ~~| /0 ::number 5 !| index)] | eq [2 2 4])
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesAStepThatIsNoCommand
        |~~ A step of a recipe is no command of a chain. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(add 1) ~(add 1)] !| tag | eq ::fn/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesACommandWithNoModifiers
        |~~ A command writes its modifiers. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(returns) ~(1)] !| tag | eq ::fn/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesAnInputWithNoPage
        |~~ An input names its page. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :by /0) ~(add by)] !| tag | eq ::fn/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesAModifierPastTheKinds
        |~~ The command of an input writes no modifier after its kinds. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number 1) ~(add by)] !| tag | eq ::fn/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesAPageThatIsNoDoc
        |~~ A page is a doc. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :by "How much." /0) ~(add by)] !| tag | eq ::fn/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesANameThatIsNoKeyword
        |~~ The name of an input is a keyword. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes "by" |~~ How much. ~~| /0) ~(add by)] !| tag | eq ::fn/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesAnInputNamedWithAPath
        |~~ The name of an input is one segment. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :by/x |~~ How much. ~~| /0) ~(1)] !| tag | eq ::fn/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesAnInputNoStepReads
        |~~ The name of an input is one a step reads. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :"a b" |~~ How much. ~~| /0) ~(1)] !| tag | eq ::fn/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesAWordOfALiteralAsAnInput
        |~~ A word of a literal is no input, which a step would read as
            the value.
        ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :null |~~ Nothing. ~~| /0) ~(1)] !| tag | eq ::fn/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesARefusalNoTagReads
        |~~ The name of a refusal is one a tag reads. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(throws :"Too big" |~~ Too big. ~~|) ~(1)] !| tag | eq ::fn/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesTheAnswerAsAnInput
        |~~ The answer is no input. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :answer |~~ An answer. ~~| /0) ~(1)] !| tag | eq ::fn/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesTheSubjectAsAnInput
        |~~ The subject is no input. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :subject |~~ A subject. ~~| /0) ~(1)] !| tag | eq ::fn/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesASelectorThatIsNoPathOrQuote
        |~~ A selector is a path or a quote. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| 0) ~(add by)] !| tag | eq ::fn/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesKindsThatAreNoTags
        |~~ Kinds are tags. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 #[1]) ~(add by)] !| tag | eq ::fn/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesKindsOfEachElementTwice
        |~~ The kinds of each element stand in the vector as one tag or
            one set.
        ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 [::number ::string]) ~(add by)] !| tag | eq ::fn/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesAnEmptySetOfKindsOfTheAnswer
        |~~ The answer names one kind at least, a set of none refused by
            the chain.
        ~~|
        ~(::fn | returns |~~ A. ~~| #[] !| tag | eq ::fn/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :NameDeclaredTwiceError/refusesTwoInputsOfOneName
        |~~ Two inputs of one name are refused. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | takes :by |~~ Again. ~~| /1) ~(1)] !| tag | eq ::fn/NameDeclaredTwiceError)
    | proves :NameDeclaredTwiceError/refusesAnInvariantNamedAsTheRefusalOfKinds
        |~~ An invariant named as the refusal of its input's kinds is
            refused.
        ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | holds :by/KindNotTakenError |~~ Positive. ~~| ~(gt 0)) ~(1)] !| tag | eq ::fn/NameDeclaredTwiceError)
    | proves :NameUnderNoInputError/refusesARefusalUnderNoInput
        |~~ A refusal under a name no input takes is refused. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(throws :x/TooBigError |~~ Too big. ~~|) ~(1)] !| tag | eq ::fn/NameUnderNoInputError)
    | proves :NameUnderNoInputError/refusesAnInvariantOfNoInput
        |~~ An invariant written with no path holds of nothing. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(holds :TooBigError |~~ Too big. ~~| ~(lt 10)) ~(1)] !| tag | eq ::fn/NameUnderNoInputError)
    | proves :LawUnderNoNameError/refusesALawUnderNoName
        |~~ A law under a name the function does not declare is refused. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(proves :x/holds |~~ An x. ~~| ~(true)) ~(1)] !| tag | eq ::fn/LawUnderNoNameError)
    | proves :RecipeKindNotTakenError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no recipe. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~() 5] !| get [~(tag) ~(expected)] | eq [::fn/RecipeKindNotTakenError #[::builtin ::null ::quote]])
    | proves :RecipeMissingError/refusesAContract
        |~~ A function with no recipe is refused at its call. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0) [3] !| tag | eq ::fn/RecipeMissingError)
    | proves :RecipeMissingError/refusesAContractCalledByName
        |~~ A contract under a label is a verb its call refuses. ~~|
        ~(:number/c (::fn | takes :x |~~ x ~~| /0) | 5 | get [~(c 1 !| tag) ~(number/c 1 !| tag)] | eq [::fn/RecipeMissingError ::fn/RecipeMissingError])
    | proves :RecipeMissingError/refusesAPrimitivePutIntoAFunctionOfItsOwn
        |~~ The primitive of a verb put into a function of its own runs
            nothing, the refusal naming the address of the verb.
        ~~|
        ~({:a 1} | apply (::fn | impl (::vec/first | binding | value | get /1)) [] !| get [~(tag) ~(of)] | eq [::fn/RecipeMissingError ::vec/first])
    | tells :call
        |~~ The call of a function `apply` runs or whose inputs `fill`
            reads, which no verb names: a refusal of its subject, its
            args, its inputs, its answer or its invariants is named under
            it, `::fn/call/by/KindNotTakenError`, as a verb's is named
            under its address, and reads this page, the pages of the roles
            staying with the function; a function named under a label
            names them under its address, where each reads its own.
        ~~|
    | proves :call/refusesArgsPastItsInputs
        |~~ Args past its arity are refused. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~(add by)) [1 2] !| tag | eq ::fn/call/ArgsBeyondInputsError)
    | proves :call/refusesAnInputLeftOut
        |~~ An input the args leave out is refused. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~(add by)) !| tag | eq ::fn/call/by/NotGivenError)
    | proves :call/pagesTheRefusalsNamedUnderIt
        |~~ A refusal named under the call reads its page. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | impl ~(add by)) ["x"] !| doc | eq (::fn/call | doc))
    | impl ::builtin{}

:fn/on
  |~~ Names the subject of a function, its page and the kinds it serves,
      `::fn | on |~~ A number. ~~| ::number`: a function `apply` runs
      serves a subject of those kinds alone, and a verb serves them beside
      the values of its label, the noun's own tag name for a verb of the
      noun itself.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on
        |~~ The noun itself, which starts the function, or a function. ~~|
        ::tag
    | takes :modifiers
        |~~ The modifiers of the command as written: the page of the subject, a
            doc, and the kinds it serves, a tag or a set of one tag or more, any
            value where none is written.
        ~~|
        ~(it)
    | returns |~~ The function with its subject. ~~| ::fn
    | throws :SubjectNotFnError
        |~~ `on` names the subject of the noun's function, `::fn | on …`,
            or of a function.
        ~~|
    | proves :servesTheKindsItNames
        |~~ A function serves a subject of the kinds `on` names and
            refuses another under its call, the kinds its `:expected`.
        ~~|
        ~(:f (::fn | on |~~ A number. ~~| ::number | impl ~(add 1))
          | get [~(5 | apply f) ~("x" | apply f !| get [~(tag) /expected])]
          | eq [6 [::fn/call/SubjectKindNotTakenError #[::number]]])
    | proves :pagesTheSubjectOfAVerb
        |~~ The page of the subject is the page of its node under the
            verb.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/inc (::fn | on |~~ The number to raise. ~~| | impl ~(add 1)) | ::number/inc/subject | doc | content | trim | eq "The number to raise.")
    | proves :SubjectNotFnError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | on |~~ A number. ~~| !| tag | eq ::fn/on/SubjectNotFnError))
    ::builtin{}]

:fn/takes
  |~~ Adds an input to a function: its name, its page, its selector over
      the args, and the kinds it holds where they are given, a value of
      none refused under the name of the input,
      `::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number`. The selector is a
      path into the args, read strictly, `/0` the first and `/0/by` the key
      `by` of a map handed first; one of two forms, read as written and
      never run, `~(query /0 1)` the first or, where the call gives none,
      one, and `~(it)` the args whole, which no verb of those names reaches;
      or any other quote, code that reads them.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on
        |~~ The noun itself, which starts the function, or a function. ~~|
        ::tag
    | takes :modifiers
        |~~ The modifiers of the command as written: the name of the input, a
            keyword its recipe reads as a step, of one segment, neither `answer`
            nor `subject`, which the chain lays itself, nor a word of a literal;
            its page, a doc; its selector over the args, a path or a quote;
            and its kinds, a tag or a set of one tag or more, or a vector of one
            of them for the kinds of each element, any value where none is
            written.
        ~~|
        ~(it)
    | returns
        |~~ The function with the input after the ones it held. ~~|
        ::fn
    | throws :SubjectNotFnError
        |~~ `takes` builds from the noun, `::fn | takes …`, or a function.
        ~~|
    | proves :addsAnInput
        |~~ An input is added by its name, its page and its selector. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | inputs | map /name | eq [:by])
    | proves :holdsTheKinds
        |~~ An input of kinds refuses a value of none under its name. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | impl ~(add by)) ["x"] !| tag | eq ::fn/call/by/KindNotTakenError)
    | proves :holdsTheValueAsItIsGiven
        |~~ An input holds the value as the call gives it, its tags with it,
            where the walk of its tags reaches one of its kinds.
        ~~|
        ~(:Width |~~ A width. ~~|
          | 5
          | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | impl ~(by | tag)) [::Width#3]
          | eq ::Width)
    | proves :pagesTheRefusalOfItsKindsByItsInput
        |~~ The refusal the kinds of an input name reads the page of the
            input where `throws` gives it no page.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | impl ~(add by))
          | ::number/plus/by/KindNotTakenError
          | doc
          | content
          | trim
          | eq "How much.")
    | proves :holdsEachElementAsItIsGiven
        |~~ An input of the kinds of each element holds each as the call
            gives it, where the walk of its tags reaches one of the kinds.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :xs |~~ Values. ~~| /0 [::number] | impl ~(xs)) [[1 ::Width#2]] | eq [1 ::Width#2])
    | proves :keepsASetOfElements
        |~~ A set an input of the kinds of each element holds stays a set.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :xs |~~ Values. ~~| /0 [::number] | impl ~(xs)) [#[2 1]] | eq #[1 2])
    | proves :holdsAnyElement
        |~~ The kinds `::any` of each element ask for a vector alone. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :xs |~~ Values. ~~| /0 [::any] | impl ~(xs)) [[1 "a"]] | eq [1 "a"])
    | proves :refusesAnElementOfNoneOfItsKinds
        |~~ An element of none of the kinds is refused with its index. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :xs |~~ Values. ~~| /0 [::number] | impl ~(xs)) [[1 "a"]]
          !| get [~(tag) /index]
          |  eq [::fn/call/xs/ElementKindNotTakenError 1])
    | proves :refusesNoVectorOfElements
        |~~ A value that is no vector is refused where the input names the
            kinds of each element.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :xs |~~ Values. ~~| /0 [::number] | impl ~(xs)) [5] !| tag | eq ::fn/call/xs/KindNotTakenError)
    | proves :pagesTheRefusalOfTheKindsOfEachElementByItsInput
        |~~ The refusal the kinds of each element name reads the page of
            the input where `throws` gives it no page.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/w (::fn | takes :xs |~~ Values. ~~| /0 [::number] | impl ~(xs))
          | ::number/w/xs/ElementKindNotTakenError
          | doc
          | content
          | trim
          | eq "Values.")
    | proves :readsAKeyOfAMap
        |~~ A path into the args reads an input by its key. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0/by | impl ~(add by)) [{:by 3}] | eq 8)
    | proves :givesADefault
        |~~ A selector written as `query` gives a default. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| ~(query /0 1) | impl ~(add by)) | eq 6)
    | proves :readsTheArgsWhole
        |~~ A selector written `~(it)` reads the args whole. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :xs |~~ Values. ~~| ~(it) | impl ~(xs | count)) [1 2 3] | eq 3)
    | proves :readsItsFormsByNoVerbOfTheirNames
        |~~ A verb named `query` reaches no selector written in its form. ~~|
        ~(:vec/query ~(99) | 5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| ~(query /0 1) | impl ~(add by)) | eq 6)
    | proves :answersTheFailureOfItsSelector
        |~~ A selector that reads the args by code and fails answers its
            failure.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| ~(first | sub "x") | impl ~(add by)) [3]
          !| tag
          |  eq ::number/sub/subtrahend/KindNotTakenError)
    | proves :refusesAStepWrittenForItsQuote
        |~~ A modifier computed at the call that failed, where the input
            that reads it takes a quote, is refused under its
            kinds.
        ~~|
        ~(:vec/each (::fn | takes :code |~~ The code. ~~| /0 ::quote | impl ~(map code))
          | [1 2]
          | each (add 1)
          !| tag
          |  eq ::vec/each/code/KindNotTakenError)
    | proves :refusesAStepWrittenForAQuoteOfTheArgsAtItsIndex
        |~~ Where the input that reads the args whole takes quotes, a
            modifier that failed is refused at its index.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/w (::fn | takes :cs |~~ Codes. ~~| ~(it) [::quote] | impl ~(1))
          | 5
          | w ~(add 1) (get /x)
          !| get [~(tag) ~(index)]
          | eq [::number/w/cs/ElementKindNotTakenError 1])
    | proves :SubjectNotFnError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 !| tag | eq ::fn/takes/SubjectNotFnError)
    | proves :handsWhatItWritesToTheChain
        |~~ A name that is no keyword is refused by the chain, which holds
            what each command writes.
        ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes "by" |~~ How much. ~~| /0 !| get [~(tag) ~(index) ~(actualValue)] | eq [::fn/CommandNotTakenError 0 "by"]))
    ::builtin{}]

:fn/returns
  |~~ Names the answer of a function, its page and its kinds, the tag or
      the set of tags it is brought to,
      `::fn | returns |~~ The sum. ~~| ::number`: an answer whose walk
      reaches one of the kinds is the value it reaches, one that reaches
      none is put under the one kind named, and one of none of the kinds
      is refused under the answer.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on
        |~~ The noun itself, which starts the function, or a function. ~~|
        ::tag
    | takes :modifiers
        |~~ The modifiers of the command as written: the page of the answer, a
            doc, and its kinds, a tag or a set of one tag or more.
        ~~|
        ~(it)
    | returns |~~ The function with its answer. ~~| ::fn
    | throws :SubjectNotFnError
        |~~ `returns` names the answer of the noun's function,
            `::fn | returns …`, or of a function.
        ~~|
    | proves :bringsTheAnswerUnderItsKind
        |~~ An answer of another kind is refused under the answer of the
            call, the kind its `:expected`.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | returns |~~ A number. ~~| ::number | impl ~("x")) !| get [~(tag) /expected] | eq [::fn/call/answer/KindNotTakenError #[::number]])
    | proves :refusesAnAnswerOfNoneOfItsKinds
        |~~ An answer of none of several kinds is refused under the answer
            of the call.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | returns |~~ A number or a string. ~~| #[::number ::string] | impl ~(gt 1))
          !| get [~(tag) /actualValue]
          |  eq [::fn/call/answer/KindNotTakenError true])
    | proves :passesTheFailureOfTheRecipe
        |~~ A recipe that fails answers its failure, which no kind brings.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | returns |~~ A number. ~~| ::number | impl ~(get /nope)) !| tag | eq ::path/SubjectHasNoPartsError)
    | proves :namesTheAnswerOfAVerb
        |~~ The answer of a function named under a label is the answer of
            the verb.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/half (::fn | returns |~~ The half. ~~| ::number | impl ~(div 2)) | ::number/half | manifest | has ::number/half/answer)
    | proves :SubjectNotFnError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | returns |~~ A number. ~~| ::number !| tag | eq ::fn/returns/SubjectNotFnError))
    ::builtin{}]

:fn/throws
  |~~ Names a refusal of a function, its page and the kind of its facts,
      `::fn | throws :TooBigError |~~ A sum past a bound. ~~| ~(wires :bound |~~ The bound. ~~| ::number)`,
      under the subject, an input or the answer where it is written with a
      path, the page of the refusal the kinds of an input name among them;
      under a label it is a refusal of the verb. The facts are the commands
      of the kind of the refusal, a quote, each `wires` a fact read by the
      key of its name in the facts of the error, and `throws` builds the
      kind of them, its payload the error the refusal raises, an `::error`,
      and its wiring ending with `trace`, so the error at rest of the
      refusal answers each fact by its name, `!| bound`. A refusal the
      rules of the chain lay, of the kinds of an input, of an input left
      out, of args past the inputs and of a subject of another label, takes
      the kind of its family, `::fn/KindNotTakenError`, and its `throws`
      writes its page alone. A refusal that shares the kind of another names
      it by its tag instead of the quote,
      `| throws :ConditionKindNotTakenError |~~ … ~~| ::fn/KindNotTakenError`,
      its error at rest closed by the kind that closes the refusal the tag
      names.
      ::link~(::kind/wires | doc) ::link~(::fn/KindNotTakenError | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on
        |~~ The noun itself, which starts the function, or a function. ~~|
        ::tag
    | takes :modifiers
        |~~ The modifiers of the command as written: the name of the refusal, a
            keyword read as a tag, under the subject, an input or the answer
            where it is written with a path; its page, a doc; and the kind of
            its facts, a quote of `wires` or the tag of the refusal whose kind
            it shares, none where it holds its trace alone.
        ~~|
        ~(it)
    | returns |~~ The function with the refusal. ~~| ::fn
    | throws :SubjectNotFnError
        |~~ `throws` names a refusal of the noun's function,
            `::fn | throws …`, or of a function.
        ~~|
    | proves :declaresARefusalOfAVerb
        |~~ A refusal of a function named under a label is a refusal of
            the verb.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | throws :TooBigError |~~ A sum past a bound. ~~| | impl ~(add by))
          | ::number/plus
          | manifest
          | has ::number/plus/TooBigError)
    | proves :pagesTheRefusalOfKinds
        |~~ A refusal the kinds of an input name takes the page `throws`
            gives it.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | throws :by/KindNotTakenError |~~ By is a number. ~~| | impl ~(add by))
          | ::number/plus/by/KindNotTakenError
          | doc
          | content
          | trim
          | eq "By is a number.")
    | proves :SubjectNotFnError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | fn/throws :E |~~ An e. ~~| !| tag | eq ::fn/throws/SubjectNotFnError))
    ::builtin{}]

:fn/holds
  |~~ Writes an invariant of the subject, an input or the answer, a quote
      under `::invariant`: the refusal of a value that breaks it, named
      under the subject, the input or the answer, its page, and the
      condition the value answers true to,
      `| holds :by/TooBigError |~~ Under a hundred. ~~| ~(lt 100)`. An
      invariant of the subject holds of the subject the walk served, before
      the inputs are read, `| holds :subject/NotIntegerError |~~ A whole number. ~~| ~(eq (floor))`.
      ::link~(::invariant | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on
        |~~ The noun itself, which starts the function, or a function. ~~|
        ::tag
    | takes :modifiers
        |~~ The modifiers of the command as written: the name of the refusal of
            a value that breaks it, a keyword read as a tag, written with a path
            under the subject, an input or the answer, `:by/TooBigError`; its
            page, a doc; and the condition the value answers true to, a quote.
        ~~|
        ~(it)
    | returns |~~ The function with the invariant. ~~| ::fn
    | throws :SubjectNotFnError
        |~~ `holds` writes an invariant of the noun's function,
            `::fn | holds …`, or of a function.
        ~~|
    | proves :writesAnInvariantOfAVerb
        |~~ An invariant of a function named under a label is a node of
            the verb.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | holds :by/TooBigError |~~ Under a hundred. ~~| ~(lt 100) | impl ~(add by))
          | 5
          | plus 500
          !| tag
          |  eq ::number/plus/by/TooBigError)
    | proves :writesAnInvariantOfTheSubject
        |~~ An invariant of the subject of a verb refuses a subject that
            breaks it under the verb.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/inc (::fn | holds :subject/NotAboveZeroError |~~ Above zero. ~~| ~(gt 0) | impl ~(add 1)) | get [~(5 | inc) ~(-5 | inc !| tag)] | eq [6 ::number/inc/subject/NotAboveZeroError])
    | proves :passesAValueThatKeepsIt
        |~~ A value that keeps every invariant of its input goes on to the
            recipe.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | holds :by/TooBigError |~~ Under a hundred. ~~| ~(lt 100) | impl ~(add by)) [3] | eq 8)
    | proves :SubjectNotFnError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | fn/holds :x/E |~~ An e. ~~| ~(true) !| tag | eq ::fn/holds/SubjectNotFnError))
    ::builtin{}]

:fn/proves
  |~~ Writes a law of a function, a quote under `::law`, the claim its
      name makes, its page and the query that proves it,
      `| proves :addsBy |~~ Five and three is eight. ~~| ~(5 | plus 3 | eq 8)`;
      under a label it is a law of the verb, which `laws` and `runLaws`
      read, and a name written with a path lays it under the subject, an
      input, a refusal, a fact or the answer, the refusal an input's kinds
      name among them.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on
        |~~ The noun itself, which starts the function, or a function. ~~|
        ::tag
    | takes :modifiers
        |~~ The modifiers of the command as written: the name of the law, a
            keyword read as a tag, under a name declared before it where it is
            written with a path; its page, the claim it proves, a doc; and the
            query that proves the claim, answering `true`, a quote.
        ~~|
        ~(it)
    | returns |~~ The function with the law. ~~| ::fn
    | throws :SubjectNotFnError
        |~~ `proves` writes a law of the noun's function,
            `::fn | proves …`, or of a function.
        ~~|
    | proves :declaresALawOfAVerb
        |~~ A law of a function named under a label is a law of the verb.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | proves :addsBy |~~ Five and three is eight. ~~| ~(5 | plus 3 | eq 8) | impl ~(add by))
          | ::number/plus
          | runLaws
          | map /ok
          | eq [true])
    | proves :liesUnderTheRefusalOfAnInput
        |~~ A law written under the refusal an input's kinds name lies
            under it.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | proves :by/KindNotTakenError/refusesAString |~~ A string is refused. ~~| ~(5 | plus "x" !| tag | eq ::number/plus/by/KindNotTakenError) | impl ~(add by))
          | ::number/plus/by/KindNotTakenError
          | runLaws
          | map /ok
          | eq [true])
    | proves :SubjectNotFnError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | fn/proves :x |~~ An x. ~~| ~(true) !| tag | eq ::fn/proves/SubjectNotFnError))
    ::builtin{}]

:fn/impl
  |~~ Gives a function its recipe, the code or the primitive that answers
      for it, `| impl ~(add by)`, and answers the function it builds,
      whatever came before it: `::fn | impl ~(add 1)` is the function of no
      commands, `::fn[~() ~(add 1)]`, which a command written after it
      joins, as after any `impl`. A recipe written alone under a label
      stays the quote it is, which its call reads as that function.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on
        |~~ The noun itself, which starts the function, or a function. ~~|
        ::tag
    | takes :recipe
        |~~ The recipe, a quote or a primitive of the host, `::builtin{}`,
            or null for a contract.
        ~~|
        /0
    | returns |~~ The function with its recipe. ~~| ::fn
    | throws :SubjectNotFnError
        |~~ `impl` gives the recipe of the noun's function,
            `::fn | impl …`, or of a function.
        ~~|
    | proves :buildsTheFunctionOfNoCommands
        |~~ Over the noun alone `impl` builds the function of no commands,
            which a command after it joins.
        ~~|
        ~(get [~(::fn | impl ~(add 1)) ~(::fn | impl ~(add 1) | takes :x |~~ x ~~| /0 | inputs | map /name)] | eq [::fn[~() ~(add 1)] [:x]])
    | proves :refusesARecipeThatIsNoCode
        |~~ A recipe that is no code is refused as the literal refuses it.
        ~~|
        ~(::fn | impl 5 !| tag | eq ::fn/RecipeKindNotTakenError)
    | proves :SubjectNotFnError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | fn/impl ~(add 1) !| tag | eq ::fn/impl/SubjectNotFnError))
    ::builtin{}]

:fn/fill
  |~~ Writes the args of a call into the head of the code of a
      function, each input a declaration with its page of the value it
      reads from them, as its call reads it, a quote among them written
      as the data it is, and answers the code:
      `::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~(add by) | fill 3`
      answers `~(:by |~~ How much. ~~| 3 | add by)`.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(takes :args
        |~~ The args, as a call holds them. ~~|
        ~(it)
    | returns |~~ The code, its inputs written at its head. ~~| ::quote
    | throws :SubjectNotFnError |~~ `fill` writes into a function. ~~|
    | throws :RecipeKindNotTakenError
        |~~ `fill` writes into code, a quote: a contract or a primitive has
            none.
        ~~|
        ~(wires :expected |~~ The kinds taken, where a value of none of them was refused. ~~| ::set
          | wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the value refused. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The value refused. ~~|)
    | proves :writesTheArgs
        |~~ The value goes into the head of the code. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~(add by) | fill 3 | eq ~(:by |~~ How much. ~~| 3 | add by))
    | proves :writesEachInput
        |~~ Each input goes into the head of the code in its order. ~~|
        ~(::fn
          | takes :a |~~ An a. ~~| /0
          | takes :b |~~ A b. ~~| /1
          | impl ~(add a | add b)
          | fill 1 2
          | eq ~(:a |~~ An a. ~~| 1 | :b |~~ A b. ~~| 2 | add a | add b))
    | proves :writesIntoTheEmptyCode
        |~~ Into the empty code the value goes as its one declaration. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~() | fill 3 | eq ~(:by |~~ How much. ~~| 3))
    | proves :writesADocAsTheValue
        |~~ A doc goes into the head of the code in parentheses, the value
            of its input.
        ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :d |~~ A doc. ~~| /0 | impl ~(d | content) | fill |~~ x ~~|
          | eq ~(:d |~~ A doc. ~~| (|~~ x ~~|) | d | content))
    | proves :holdsTheKinds
        |~~ A value of none of the kinds of its input is refused. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | impl ~(add by) | fill "x" !| tag | eq ::fn/call/by/KindNotTakenError)
    | proves :SubjectNotFnError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no function. ~~|
        ~(5 | fill 3 !| tag | eq ::fn/fill/SubjectNotFnError)
    | proves :RecipeKindNotTakenError/refusesAContract
        |~~ A function with no recipe is refused. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | fill 3 !| get [~(tag) ~(expected) ~(trace | last | path)] | eq [::fn/fill/RecipeKindNotTakenError #[::quote] /1]))
    ::builtin{}]

:fn/inputs
  |~~ Answers the inputs of a function, each a map of its name, its page,
      its selector and its kinds as written, null where it names none.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(returns |~~ The inputs, a map for each. ~~| ::vec
    | throws :SubjectNotFnError |~~ `inputs` reads a function. ~~|
    | proves :readsTheInputs
        |~~ The inputs come out by their names. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :a |~~ An a. ~~| /0 | returns |~~ A sum. ~~| ::number | impl ~(a) | inputs | map /name | eq [:a])
    | proves :readsTheKindsAsWritten
        |~~ The kinds of an input come out as written. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :a |~~ An a. ~~| /0 ::number | takes :b |~~ A b. ~~| /1 | inputs | map /kinds | eq [::number null])
    | proves :SubjectNotFnError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no function. ~~|
        ~(5 | inputs !| tag | eq ::fn/inputs/SubjectNotFnError))
    ::builtin{}]
